  "narrative": {
    "intro": "V2X Aerospace has $1.4B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. V2X Aerospace has won 89 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $15.2M. Obligations fell 11.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations rose from FY21 $958M to FY25 $1.5B, then show a partial FY26 total of $1.4B. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $1B, followed by the General Services Administration at $287M and the Department of Justice at $27.2M. Other notable buyers include the Department of Homeland Security at $10.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $2.7M. Other Support Activities for Air Transportation is the largest market at $953M, and Engineering Services is next at $329M. Aircraft Manufacturing accounts for $33.7M in obligations this fiscal year. Smaller professional and scientific services markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $20.8M and Other Scientific and Technical Consulting Services at $20.1M. All figures are fiscal-year-to-date contract obligations unless otherwise noted.",
    "sections": [
